        "original_id": "fe75533c-70a4-5841-8265-f5d3b4a7e311",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Regency Road, Adelaide; Klemzig; Dudley Park; Croydon electoral district; Kilkenny; Broadview\n- Topics: Road geography; suburb boundaries; electoral district coverage\n\nFacts:\n- Regency Road in Adelaide is located about 6 km north of the city centre.\n- Regency Road runs from Arndale Shopping Centre in Kilkenny in the west to Broadview in the east, then continues as Muller Road to North East Road in Klemzig.\n- Klemzig is a suburb of Adelaide in the City of Port Adelaide Enfield.\n- Dudley Park is bordered to the north by Regency Road, to the south by Simpson Avenue, to the east by the Adelaide-Gawler railway line, and to the west by a north-south line from the Harrison Road-Simpson Avenue intersection to Regency Road.\n- The electoral district of Croydon includes Dudley Park, Kilkenny, and parts of Ferryden Park, along with Croydon, Allenby Gardens, Beverley, Brompton, Bowden, West Croydon, Croydon Park, Devon Park, Flinders Park, Hindmarsh, West Hindmarsh, Renown Park, Ridleyton, Welland, Woodville Gardens, and Woodville Park.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
